From 61b8b2aeb88a9a3378c2e6bd2fa7760b503e41a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:41:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] avalanche(v2): only final block votes move the finalization
 tip

v2/043 removed the Finalized/Invalid filter at the top of the post-vote
loop in registerVotes when it added treasury contenders, which also act
on Accepted and Rejected. Every Accepted or Rejected block update then
fell through to "the block index can only be finalized" and became
finalizationTip. IsWorthPolling then treated the block as an ancestor of
the finalization tip and dropped its vote record. A rejected block was
never polled again, so it could not be re-accepted
(abc_p2p_avalanche_voting). Also, Accepted/Rejected batch updates were
marked as conflicts.

Restore the filter after the treasury branch.

Regression: processor_tests/vote_item_register<BlockProvider> fails 129
checks without this and passes with it.

Tier: V2 (fixup to v2/043)
---
 src/avalanche/processor.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/avalanche/processor.cpp b/src/avalanche/processor.cpp
index 2a0fa4561f..b864c56635 100644
--- a/src/avalanche/processor.cpp
+++ b/src/avalanche/processor.cpp
@@ -766,6 +766,14 @@ bool Processor::registerVotes(NodeId nodeid, const Response &response,
             continue;
         }
 
+        // Treasury contenders also act on Accepted and Rejected. Everything
+        // below only acts on a final outcome: an Accepted or Rejected block
+        // is not a finalization tip, and a batch is only in conflict once
+        // it has been invalidated.
+        if (status != VoteStatus::Finalized && status != VoteStatus::Invalid) {
+            continue;
+        }
+
         if (const auto *batch = std::get_if<const MempoolBatchVoteItem>(&item)) {
             if (update.getStatus() == VoteStatus::Finalized) {
                 finalizeMempoolBatch(batch->GetId());
